      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2777671/8/tests/unit/java/com/android/server/connectivityservice/CSLocalAgentTests.kt#137 is a good example. It allows to replace code like\n\n    val cb \u003d TestableNetworkCallback()\n    cm.requestNetwork(NetworkRequest.Builder().\n     .addTransportType()\n     .addWhateverIsNeededForThisNetwork\n     .build(),\n     cb)\n    val agent \u003d Agent()\n    cm.unregisterNetworkAgent\n\nWith\n\n    fun keepScore \u003d NetworkScore.Builder.setKeepConnectedReason(FOR_TEST).build()\n    val agent \u003d Agent(score \u003d keepScore)\n\nFor tests that have a lot of similar agents it is really difficult to craft the requests correctly and it is a lot more fiddly. This just makes it so that your agent doesn\u0027t disconnect while in the test until you say so, which is a lot easier to read/understand.",
